    "notes": "Algorithm: (1) split on space into words, on '-' into syllables. (2) A syllable whose letters are all uppercase is stressed; the first in a word gets primary, any later one secondary. (3) Lowercase, then at the cursor take the first rule in `rules` whose grapheme matches (list is longest-first); a letter that no rule matches makes the whole respelling None, it is never skipped. In a stressed syllable `stressed_rules` override `rules` for the same grapheme; `r_link_rules` override both when the grapheme ends a stressed syllable and the next syllable of the word starts with a, e, i, o or u (FAR-ingks, KAR-uh-teen, HUR-ee). (4) Put the stress mark at the start of the stressed syllable's IPA, before its onset (ˈfæɹɪŋks); `vowel_symbols` lets an adapter move it to the nucleus. (5) Join syllables with no separator, words with one space. Plain y is the vowel aɪ (SY-kul, nye); consonant j comes only from the y+vowel graphemes (yoo, yuh, yah, ...). Not modelled: yod-dropping (ew/yoo keep j), t-flapping, secondary stress for unmarked syllables, vowel reduction beyond uh/u/er/ur/ir. Compact form: no length marks (ɑ i u ɔ are long in Piper), NURSE vowel is ɜɹ (espeak says ɜː before a consonant, ɜːɹ before a vowel). ɡ is U+0261; ɚ is one symbol; tʃ dʒ aɪ eɪ oʊ ɔɪ aʊ are two symbols each."
